  "agent": "conformance.absorbed.Absorbed",
  "doc": "A fan-out whose iterations score elements, with a fallback for the ones that\ncome back unusable.\n\nThe failure this case pins is **an answer that did not match its declared\ntype** — one of the four things `else` catches, and the only one a 0.3\ncassette can hold for a model call, because `Interaction` records a value and\nhas no field for an error. The recorded answer for the second element is not\nan `int`, so both backends reject it, both use the stated fallback, and both\nmust say so in the same place in the event stream.\n\nA fan-out rather than a straight line, because the point of the feature is\nthat the *other* elements' work survives: a run that lost one element used to\nspend the whole fan-out and return nothing.",
  "inputs": {
    "items": "string[]"
  },
  "outputs": {
    "digest": "artifact<json>"
  },
